---
description: Authoring notes in content/notes and keeping drafts unpublished
globs: content/notes/**
alwaysApply: false
---

Notes are MDX files. Copy `content/notes/_template.mdx` to `content/notes/<slug>.mdx`. The filename is the URL slug: lowercase kebab-case, no date in the name. Files starting with `_` are ignored by `lib/notes.ts`.

Required frontmatter: `title` (string), `date` (the day the note was added, `YYYY-MM-DD`, quoted), `summary` (string), `tags` (array of strings, lowercase, hyphenated), `draft` (boolean). The build fails if a required field is missing or the wrong type. The index, tag pages, and the note show that day as “Added 1 Nov 2026”. Optional `updated` (`YYYY-MM-DD`) is a revision day; when it is set, those places also show “Updated …”. Optional: `image`.

Every new note ships with an illustrated SVG cover at `public/note-covers/<slug>.svg`, in the site’s style: flat shapes on a 1200×750 canvas, the Lab palette (navy `#0A1045`, cyan `#00C2D1`, yellow `#F9E900`, peach `#F6AF65`, pink `#ED33B9`) with paper `#F3EEE6`, Thames `#1E4A42`, and clay `#C45C32`, matching the covers already in that folder. Set `cover` to `/note-covers/<slug>.svg` and `coverAlt` to a description of the drawing. When `cover` is set, the file has to exist under `public/` (the loader also accepts webp, jpg, png, avif, or gif). `coverAlt` is only valid together with `cover`. The notes index shows `cover` on the card. A note without one gets a colour pattern from its title and tags. A new note still includes the SVG. The note page shows `cover` at the top, and the social card uses it.

Leave `draft: true` unless Jake asked for the note to go live in that pull request. Drafts render in `next dev` and on Vercel preview, and they are omitted from production, `/feed.xml`, and `/sitemap.xml`.

Write about technology, the apps, or something Jake is exploring. Do not invent biographical facts. How-to: `docs/adding-a-note.md`. Full schema: `AGENTS.md`.

Every pull request skips screenshots. Run `npm run lint`, `npm run typecheck`, and `npm run build` before pushing. When the Vercel preview is ready, include the preview URL of each changed page in the pull request and in the report. A note’s URL is `https://<preview>/notes/<slug>`. Also name the title, date, summary, and whether it is still a draft.
